;; spec:   §6 (types §2.11, §6.14, §8.7)
;; expect: reject
;; error:  weak of an Option is not allowed
;; A weak reference to an Option value is a type error (Decided, owner,
;; 2026-09-27). An Option has no object of its own to observe: an
;; (Option str) is a nullable pointer to the string, so its weak box
;; would be the payload's and its upgrade could not tell "o died" from
;; "o was nil"; (weak nil) would read the header of a null pointer; and
;; a heap-enum Option such as (some 5) is a fresh object at each
;; (some ..), whose identity no program can hold on to. The weak
;; reference is taken of the object inside instead (adversary finding
;; 002, which expected (some (some "ab")) back).
(defun main () -> i64
  (let ((o (some (str-concat "a" "b"))) (w (weak o)))
    (match @w ((some (some x)) (str-len x)) ((some nil) 1) (nil 2))))
